# The box: Overflow shrink makes the letters of a text smaller until it fits, and Overflow clip cuts what sticks out of a box.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: The box · Overflow
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: row
			Gap: 16
			Vertical: top
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 20 0
		For style: fixed
			Box:
				Width: 150
				Height: 36
				Padding: 4 6
				Background: tint
				Border: 0 0 0 2
				Border color: accent
			Typography:
				Size: 14
				Line height: 120%
	Section:
		Text: The box
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Overflow
		Paragraph: What does not fit in a box is an error, unless the box asks for something else. `Overflow: shrink`, in a box with text, lowers the `Size` half a point at a time until the text fits, without going below `Min size`. `Overflow: clip`, in a box without text, cuts what sticks out of its padding box.
			Style: intro
		Text: Three boxes of 150 × 36 with Size: 14 and Overflow: shrink
			Style: label
		Stack:
			Style: row
			Item:
				Text: Ana Ruiz
					Style: fixed
					Box:
						Overflow: shrink
			Item:
				Text: Maria del Carmen Vidal
					Style: fixed
					Box:
						Overflow: shrink
			Item:
				Text: Maria del Carmen Vidal Soler de la Fuente
					Style: fixed
					Box:
						Overflow: shrink
		Text: Min size: 11  (the letters never go below 11: a longer name would be an error)
			Style: label
		Text: Maria del Carmen Vidal Soler
			Style: fixed
			Box:
				Overflow: shrink
				Margin: 0 0 20 0
			Typography:
				Min size: 11
		Text: Overflow: clip  (the circle sticks out of the card and is cut at its edge)
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Box:
				Width: 260
				Height: 90
				Background: tint
				Corner radius: 8
				Overflow: clip
			Overlay:
				Offset: -40 -40 auto auto
				Block:
					Box:
						Width: 120
						Height: 120
						Corner radius: 50%
						Background: #E9A23B
